UNIT fireOrder
KIND FUNCTIONAL
FIDELITY spec
SIG fireOrder(events, clock) -> Promise<Array>
DESCRIPTION `events` is an array of { value, delay } objects. The unit arms one timer per
DESCRIPTION event and returns the values in the order their timers FIRE.
DESCRIPTION Timers are armed through the caller-supplied clock, which offers exactly two calls:
DESCRIPTION   clock.setTimer(fn, ms) -> handle   run `fn` after `ms` of VIRTUAL time
DESCRIPTION   clock.clearTimer(handle)           disarm a timer that has not yet fired
DESCRIPTION The clock owns time and the harness advances it. The unit MUST NOT use setTimeout,
DESCRIPTION setInterval, Date, performance.now, or any other real-time source, and must not
DESCRIPTION compute the answer by sorting instead of by arming timers — the firing is the work.
DESCRIPTION Export the function as the DEFAULT export. No imports of any kind.
INVARIANT the result holds every event's value, ordered by ascending `delay`.
INVARIANT TIES: two events with the SAME delay fire in the order they appear in `events`.
INVARIANT   Arm them in array order and this falls out; deriving order from `delay` alone
INVARIANT   loses it, and the loss is invisible whenever no two delays happen to be equal.
INVARIANT every event arms exactly ONE timer, and every armed timer FIRES — the unit clears
INVARIANT   none of them. A result that is correct with no timer armed is not this unit.
INVARIANT delays are measured from the moment the unit is called, not from each other.
INVARIANT the returned promise resolves only after the LAST timer has fired.
INVARIANT an empty events array returns [] without arming any timer.
